; The well-known-tag registry default: tag 258 is the IANA set tag, so a `#6.258` that directly
; wraps a homogeneous occurrence collection carries set semantics — uniqueness — and defaults to
; `@duplicates reject` when the author wrote NO explicit directive. The alias target is the
; uniqueness twin (`OrderedSet` / `NonEmptyOrderedSet`), exactly as an explicit `@duplicates reject`
; would produce (see tag_set_reject.cddl); the registry merely supplies that policy as the default a
; per-rule directive can still override. This is a decode-time behavior change: loose historical wire
; data that carried duplicate elements now fails `DuplicateKey`. The opt-out is one line of CDDL the
; consumer controls — `; @duplicates preserve` — which restores today's plain `Vec`/`NonEmptyVec`
; behavior verbatim on the wire (the multi-era byte-exact reader for duplicate-bearing data).
;
; - `default_set`    — no-directive `[*]` two-arm idiom -> `OrderedSet<u64>` by default.
; - `default_neset`  — no-directive `[+]` two-arm idiom -> `NonEmptyOrderedSet<u64>` by default (the
;                      `[+]` min-1 bound composes with uniqueness in the twin's single `TryFrom` door).
; - `single_arm`     — a single-arm MANDATORY-tag rule (`#6.258([* a])`, no untagged twin) also
;                      matches the registry shape guard, so it too defaults to reject; its tag stays a
;                      mandatory `Option<Sz>` (grammar decides the encoding record), only the inner
;                      becomes `OrderedSet<u64>`.
; - `opt_out`        — the documented opt-out recipe: an explicit `; @duplicates preserve` restores
;                      the plain `Vec<u64>` twin, byte-identical to today's no-directive output. This
;                      is the hoist-to-named-rule migration recipe the docs ship to consumers.
; - `holder`         — embeds the rules in record-field position (incl. an optional field) so the
;                      member-side (de)serialize and optional-field wrapping compile and round-trip.
default_set = #6.258([* uint]) / [* uint]
default_neset = #6.258([+ uint]) / [+ uint]
single_arm = #6.258([* uint])
opt_out = #6.258([* uint]) / [* uint] ; @duplicates preserve
holder = [s: default_set, ns: default_neset, sa: single_arm, o: opt_out]
